<!-- ==================== 6. PROPOSED METHODOLOGY ==================== -->
<h2>6. PROPOSED METHODOLOGY</h2>
<p>The processing architecture operates across six sequential phases: (1) Notice Ingestion & Multimodal OCR, (2) Text Preprocessing, (3) NLU Intent & Entity Extraction, (4) Temporal Normalization to Asia/Kolkata, (5) 5-Way Change Intelligence, and (6) Additive Priority Scoring & Cognitive Workload Partitioning.</p>
<p><strong>Mathematical Formulations:</strong></p>
<p><strong>1. Additive Invariant Priority Scoring:</strong><br>
<code>S = S_base + w_dead * f_dead + w_weight * f_weight + w_exam * f_exam + w_pen * f_pen + w_urg * f_urg + w_clust * f_clust</code><br>
Where <code>S_base = 15</code>, <code>f_dead &isin; {30, 20, 10, 5}</code>, <code>f_weight &isin; {20, 10, 5}</code>, <code>f_exam = 15</code>, <code>f_pen = 10</code>, <code>f_urg = 10</code>, and <code>f_clust = 10</code>. Score levels: Critical (&ge; 75), High (55–74), Medium (35–54), Low (&lt; 35).</p>
<p><strong>2. Temporal Timezone Resolution:</strong><br>
<code>T_IST = T_UTC + 5.5 hours</code>. Relative expressions ("tonight 11:59 PM", "next Monday") are snapped to the reference anchor date (October 31, 2026).</p>

