<!-- ==================== 13. DEPLOYMENT ==================== -->
<h2>13. DEPLOYMENT AND USER GUIDE</h2>
<p>Run locally using standard Node.js tools:</p>
<pre>
git clone &lt;repo&gt; &amp;&amp; cd "academic ai"
npm install
npx prisma db push &amp;&amp; npx prisma generate
npx tsx scripts/seed-large-dataset.ts
npm test
npm run build &amp;&amp; npm start
</pre>
<p>Application launches on <code>http://localhost:3000</code>.</p>

<!-- ==================== 14. LIMITATIONS & ETHICS ==================== -->
<h2>14. LIMITATIONS AND ETHICAL CONSIDERATIONS</h2>
<p>Current limitations include reduced accuracy on handwritten circulars and non-English scripts. The system enforces educational privacy (FERPA compliance, local SQLite persistence) and mandatory human-in-the-loop faculty approval before grades are finalized.</p>

<!-- ==================== 15. CONCLUSION ==================== -->
<h2>15. CONCLUSION AND FUTURE WORK</h2>
<p>AcademicAI resolves the challenge of university notification fragmentation through a verified pipeline delivering 76.7% classification accuracy, 93.0% entity extraction, and 94.1% temporal normalization. Future work will extend native IndicBERT multilingual support, bidirectional LMS webhooks, and peer collaborative scheduling.</p>

